│ Approve the specification?                                                   │
│                                                                              │
│ spec: {                                                                      │
│   "summary": "This specification defines reliability improvements to an      │
│ existing Spring Boot URL shortener service without altering its external     │
│ contract (endpoint paths, response shapes for success cases, validation      │
│ rules, and rate limiter behavior). The work has three parts: (1) introduce   │
│ global exception handling via a @ControllerAdvice-style mechanism so         │
│ malformed JSON request bodies, unknown short codes, and unexpected server    │
│ errors return structured JSON error bodies with correct HTTP status codes    │
│ (400, 404, 500) instead of default servlet-container or Spring Boot          │
│ Whitelabel error pages; (2) verify and, if necessary, reconfigure the        │
│ embedded H2 database to file-based persistence mode so redirect mappings and │
│ stats/click counts survive an application restart, migrating any purely      │
│ in-memory (e.g., HashMap-backed) storage for these features to H2-backed     │
│ persistence; and (3) extend the actuator `/actuator/health` endpoint to      │
│ expose a component reflecting the H2 database's connectivity/state, using    │
│ Spring Boot's built-in DataSource health indicator support. All changes must │
│ be verifiable via black-box HTTP testing, must not introduce any new         │
│ dependencies beyond already-approved starters (web, actuator, data-jpa/jdbc, │
│ H2), and must leave the rate limiter's behavior and limits fully intact.",   │
│   "functional_requirements": [                                               │
│     "FR1: The service SHALL return a structured JSON error response (not an  │
│ HTML/Whitelabel or container default page) for any request with a            │
│ malformed/unparseable JSON body, with HTTP status 400.",                     │
│     "FR2: The service SHALL return a structured JSON error response with     │
│ HTTP status 404 when a redirect or stats lookup is requested for a short     │
│ code that does not exist.",                                                  │
│     "FR3: The service SHALL return a structured JSON error response with     │
│ HTTP status 500 for any unhandled/unexpected server-side exception, without  │
│ leaking stack traces or internal class names in the response body.",         │
│     "FR4: All structured error responses SHALL include, at minimum, a        │
│ timestamp, an HTTP status code, an error/reason label, a human-readable      │
│ message, and the request path.",                                             │
│     "FR5: Structured error handling SHALL apply uniformly across all         │
│ existing endpoints (create short URL, redirect, stats) without changing the  │
│ success-path response shape, status codes, or field names of any endpoint.", │
│     "FR6: The rate limiter SHALL continue to return its existing response    │
│ (status code, headers, body) unchanged when a client is rate-limited; global │
│ error handling SHALL NOT intercept or alter rate-limit responses.",          │
│     "FR7: Short URL mappings created via the create endpoint SHALL be        │
│ persisted to the embedded H2 database (file-based storage mode, not          │
│ memory-only 'mem:' mode) such that they are retrievable via the redirect     │
│ endpoint after an application restart.",                                     │
│     "FR8: Click/visit statistics tracked by the stats endpoint SHALL be      │
│ persisted to the embedded H2 database such that previously recorded stats    │
│ values are retrievable via the stats endpoint after an application           │
│ restart.",                                                                   │
│     "FR9: The `/actuator/health` endpoint SHALL include a named health       │
│ component (e.g., 'db') reflecting the current connectivity/state of the H2   │
│ database, in addition to the existing overall status field.",                │
│     "FR10: When the database is reachable, the health endpoint's database    │
│ component status SHALL report 'UP'; when the database is unreachable or      │
│ misconfigured, it SHALL report 'DOWN', and this SHALL be reflected in the    │
│ overall aggregate status per default Spring Boot Actuator aggregation        │
│ rules.",                                                                     │
│     "FR11: No existing endpoint path, request schema, success response       │
│ schema, or validation rule SHALL change as an observable side effect of this │
│ work."                                                                       │
│   ],                                                                         │
│   "non_functional_requirements": [                                           │
│     "NFR1: No new third-party dependencies or libraries SHALL be introduced  │
│ beyond already-approved Spring Boot starters (web, actuator, data-jpa/jdbc)  │
│ and the H2 driver already present in the project.",                          │
│     "NFR2: Error handling logic SHALL add negligible latency (target: <10ms  │
│ overhead per request) compared to pre-change baseline for both success and   │
│ error paths.",                                                               │
│     "NFR3: Persistence changes SHALL not degrade redirect endpoint latency   │
│ by more than a reasonable margin (target: p95 response time increase <20ms)  │
│ compared to the prior in-memory implementation, under equivalent load.",     │
│     "NFR4: The H2 database file(s) SHALL be stored in a location that        │
│ survives normal application restarts (e.g., a configured file path within    │
│ the deployment environment), and this location SHALL be documented in        │
│ configuration.",                                                             │
│     "NFR5: Structured error responses SHALL never include raw exception      │
│ stack traces, SQL statements, or internal package/class names in the         │
│ response body returned to clients.",                                         │
│     "NFR6: The health endpoint change SHALL not expose sensitive connection  │
│ details (e.g., credentials, full JDBC URLs) in its default response to       │
│ unauthenticated callers, consistent with default Actuator security posture." │
│   ],                                                                         │
